      <link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/revisited/20260925-from-jungle-to-jungles-migrants-in-calais-continue-to-dream-of-uk</link>
      <description>October 2026 marks 10 years since the Calais "Jungle" in northern France was dismantled by French police. The camp was home to thousands of migrants who wanted to cross the Channel and reach the UK. A decade on, migrants continue to dream of reaching British shores and the "Jungle" has been replaced by many smaller jungles scattered along the northern French coastline. FRANCE 24's Pauline Godart, Claire Paccalin and Mohamed Farhat report. Fuente: France 24 - English.</description>
